# REACH, CLEAR TABLE — the first task in this family that can actually TRAIN.
#
# The same goal as `so101_reach_brick`. The difference is one line: NO FREE
# SLOT IS ACTIVE, so the family's three props stay parked instead of being
# placed on the table.
#
# ## ⚠⚠ WHY THAT DIFFERENCE EXISTS, AND WHAT IT IS HIDING
#
# A free slot that is ACTIVE has to be PLACED at every episode reset, and on
# the GPU training path nothing places it. `_reset_env_lane` restores the
# composed scene's `qpos0`, which for a free slot is its PARK pose — 50 m up —
# and only INACTIVE slots are pinned there afterwards by
# `So101TabletopConfig.pre_step_full_gpu` (Gap D). An active prop therefore
# starts every training episode in the sky and FALLS for the whole horizon,
# with its qpos and qvel in the observation the policy is learning from.
#
# The host DOES place them — `tasks/sampler.sample_placements` +
# `tasks/reset.reset_slots` — which is why the eval and viewer paths work and
# why this was invisible until something tried to train. Closing it means
# device-side placement in `init_qpos_gpu`, and that needs a per-lane channel
# saying which region each free slot inits into (the tape carries the GOAL's
# regions, not the INIT's). Until then `so101_reach_brick`, `so101_lift_brick`
# and `so101_gather_bricks` are authorable, evaluable and NOT trainable.
#
# ⚠ SO THIS FILE IS A SMOKE TASK, NOT A BENCHMARK. It validates the stack —
# observation, sparse reward, success termination, the SAC wiring and the
# per-task rate — on the one task shape that needs no placement. Its start
# distribution is the arm's reset noise alone (0.05 rad per joint), which is
# real but narrow. Do not read a high success rate here as "the family is
# solved".
schema_version=1
task=so101_reach_clear
family=so101_tabletop
language=Move the gripper over the table

# ⚠ IDENTICAL TO `so101_reach_brick`'s, deliberately — the two differ ONLY in
# what is on the table, so a rate measured here and a rate measured there are
# comparable once placement lands.
goal=AtRegion(robot_gripperframe, table_top)

# ⚠⚠ ONE ACTIVE SLOT, AND IT IS THE STATIC ONE. `validate_task_against_family`
# requires an `init=` for every active FREE slot and there are none here, so
# this file has no `init=` at all — which is also what makes it trainable.
# The table is a fixture: it carries its pose in the `.family` and needs no
# placement, and the goal's region sits on its surface.
active=table
